From: Aveldistarna <Aveldistarna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:56:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] sched/deadline: skip dl_server_start on isolated CPUs

On a CPU isolated with isolcpus= and nohz_full=, the fair server
(dl_server) is still started when a task is enqueued there. On a DE10-Nano
(Cyclone V, CPU1 isolated for an EVL out-of-band loop), the loop on CPU1
was stalled for 13-30 us at 0.95 s and 1.95 s after it started, each time
with a reschedule IPI and a function-call IPI to CPU1.

Do not start the server on isolated CPUs. With this change, three 10 s runs
of the loop had no stall over 10 us and no reschedule or function-call IPI
to CPU1, and CPU0 kept running normally.

Side effect: fair tasks on an isolated CPU lose the fair server's
protection against RT starvation.
---
 kernel/sched/deadline.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/deadline.c b/kernel/sched/deadline.c
index abd0fb2d839c..b2e58b35fee3 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/deadline.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/deadline.c
@@ -1628,6 +1628,10 @@ void dl_server_start(struct sched_dl_entity *dl_se)
 {
 	struct rq *rq = dl_se->rq;
 
+	/* Skip DL server on isolated CPUs to avoid 1Hz IPI noise. */
+	if (cpu_is_isolated(cpu_of(rq)))
+		return;
+
 	/*
 	 * XXX: the apply do not work fine at the init phase for the
 	 * fair server because things are not yet set. We need to improve
